Pin the C dialect OvmfPkg is compiled in, instead of inheriting gcc's.

EDK II's tools_def sets no -std, so every file is compiled in whatever
dialect the host compiler happens to default to. That was gnu17 for years;
GCC 15 defaults to gnu23. OpenCorePkg fails outright under C23 (see
internal/firmware's OpenCore build, which pins the same dialect through
upstream's own $(OCPKG_BUILD_OPTIONS) hook and therefore needs no patch).
OvmfPkg does not fail -- it compiles clean -- but it does not come out the
same:

  built with gcc 13.3.0's default (gnu17)
    OVMF_CODE.fd  195c4dcff2abf2f5aea08c290f057432704a250eab56b0b887ac0f8503ee58d2
  same tree, same compiler, -std=c2x forced
    OVMF_CODE.fd  3373692a6739121bec67d458d09a60d602b40cf5235398f208d58f28db3306b8

Measured on pet-power-plant, 2026-09-20. A host whose gcc defaults to C23
would therefore have shipped a *different firmware* than docs/decisions/0004
records, silently and with a successful build. That is worse than the
OpenCore failure, which at least announced itself.

The project pins every source input by commit and checksum but does not
pin the compiler (see decisions/0004, "The compiler"). Pinning
the dialect does not close that hole, but it removes the largest thing that
moved underneath it, and it makes two hosts' firmware checksums comparable,
which is what comparing two hosts' builds is for.

gnu17 rather than c17 because that is what these trees have always been
compiled as -- EDK II's GCC flags assume GNU extensions -- so this changes
nothing on a host that was already correct. Verified: OVMF_CODE.fd is
byte-identical with and without this patch on gcc 13.3.0.

Applied by internal/firmware's OVMF build, guarded by a grep, against the
EDK II tree its OpenCore build assembles from the pinned audk tarball.

--- a/OvmfPkg/OvmfPkgX64.dsc
+++ b/OvmfPkg/OvmfPkgX64.dsc
@@ -113,6 +113,13 @@
   GCC:*_*_*_CC_FLAGS = -D DISABLE_NEW_DEPRECATED_INTERFACES
 
   #
+  # The C dialect is an input to the build, so it is stated rather than
+  # inherited from whatever the host compiler defaults to this year.
+  # packer-plugin-macosx: assets/firmware/patches/0002-ovmf-pin-the-c-dialect.patch
+  #
+  GCC:*_*_*_CC_FLAGS = -std=gnu17
+
+  #
   # Add TDX_GUEST_SUPPORTED
   #
   MSFT:*_*_*_CC_FLAGS = /D TDX_GUEST_SUPPORTED
